<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Empress Dowager Bo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 155 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Empress Dowager Bo, born Bo Ji, was a consort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, and the mother of Emperor Wen. Originally a concubine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-bao">Wei Bao</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-wei">Western Wei</a>, she entered Liu Bang's palace after Wei Bao's defeat and bore him a son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-han">Liu Heng</a>. When he became emperor in 180 BCE she was honoured as empress dowager, and she died in 155 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/empress-dowager-bo.jpg" alt="Empress Dowager Bo" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dingar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%BA%B2%E5%B0%9D%E6%B1%A4%E8%8D%AF.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
